# Cubeless Orchestration

## Goal

- The embedded `codex/` directory is the command center for `UnrealMCP5_6_1`.
- Durable policy, coordination rules, and reusable workflows for the UE 5.6.1 MCP line live in `codex/`.
- The command center should let MCP upgrades happen inside this repository without depending on sibling repositories, submodules, or local machine state.

## Authority Model

- `codex/AGENTS.md` is the embedded operating root.
- The repository root `AGENTS.md` resolves `codex/AGENTS.md` first, then reads `codex/projects/UnrealMCP5_6_1.md`.
- Project bindings define local facts: default paths, branch expectations, engine versions, bridge ports, safe asset roots, verification gates, and local exceptions.
- If a local adapter and embedded Codex disagree, follow the stricter rule and report the conflict.

## Managed Repositories

- `UnrealMCP5_6_1`: Python MCP server, UnrealMCP plugin sample project, embedded `codex/` operating docs, and UE 5.6.1 compatibility branch.
- No sibling repository or submodule is required for routine work in this folder.
- External repositories are reference-only unless the user explicitly names them.

## Work Routing

- Start from the active checkout.
- For this MCP repository, read the root adapter, embedded Codex, and `projects/UnrealMCP5_6_1.md`.
- For MCP tooling work, read `agents/tivret-mcp.md` and `docs/workflows/mcp-upstream-update.md` when upstream sync is involved.
- For explicitly requested external project work, keep implementation and Git summaries separated by repository.

## MCP Agent Chain

- Ieta coordinates MCP direction, reviews project impact, and prepares implementation instructions.
- Tivret-MCP implements MCP tooling inside `UnrealMCP5_6_1`.
- The MCP Upstream Manager handles sync from `chongdashu/unreal-mcp`.
- The MCP Release Verifier checks MCP changes before they are treated as ready inside this repository.

## Permission Baseline

- Local Windows workstations should use the broad local-work Codex profile from `docs/policies/local-permission-profile.md`.
- New or repaired PCs may run `scripts/grant-local-workspace-full-control.ps1` from this repository if ACL repair is explicitly needed.
- Runtime sandbox settings still come from the Codex app/session launcher; filesystem ACLs do not override the active Codex permission profile.

## Upgrade Loop

1. Update or verify embedded `codex/` rules first when the requested behavior changes repository policy.
2. Update `UnrealMCP5_6_1` on its integration branch when tooling must grow.
3. Verify MCP Python import/compile checks and any targeted bridge checks.
4. Verify any explicitly requested external project smoke tests only when that external scope is part of the task.
5. Commit and push only the explicitly requested repository scope.

## Boundaries

- Do not stage generated project assets, package outputs, `_MCP_Temp`, `_MCP_Sample`, or unrelated dirty files.
- Do not rewrite public default branches unless the user explicitly approves that exact history operation.
- Do not modify credentials, secrets, remotes, account settings, or GitHub repository settings unless explicitly requested.
